  "description": "JATBIT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C134 H106 Gd8 N10 O42,2(C2 H3 N1),8(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.553-4.029 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.71-113.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd8(μ3-OH)6(L5)2(L6)8]·4CH3OH·2CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
